  "id": "EUVD-2026-32275",
  "enisaUuid": "194a6938-0990-326f-b55a-5728f81a9d09",
  "description": "A flaw was found in Samba\u2019s handling of NTFS-style reparse points on shares configured with read only = yes. Due to missing SMB-layer access checks, authenticated users with underlying filesystem write permissions may create or delete reparse point metadata through SMB operations even on read-only exports. This could allow modification of SMB-visible file behavior, including converting files into symbolic links or other reparse point types.",
